      "message": "It may optionally call onFinish(TIMEOUT). But really, vold will just stop waiting for the callback when timeout is reached.\n\nSince it is not required to call onFinish(TIMEOUT), should I still say this?\n\"When garbage collection has not completed before timeout is reached, the implementation may optionally call onFinish(TIMEOUT),\"\n\nOr, maybe I should remove \"TIMEOUT\" from Result completely, and don\u0027t have any callbacks at all if timeout?",
